//! The USB Type-C receptacle of Shouhan (Shenzhen Shouhan Technology), TYPE-C 16PIN 2MD(073): the
//! J1 and the J2 of the Easyduino ESP32-S3 board (LCSC C2765186, `catalogs/shouhan_type_c_16pin.csv`).
//! A 16-contact USB 2.0 receptacle, surface mount, right angle, with four shell legs.
//!
//! The maker's drawing (TYPE-C 16PIN 2MD(073), revision A, scale 1:8, one sheet: no date) names
//! the contacts in its "PIN ASSIGNMENTS" table: A1 and B12 `GND`, A4, A9, B4 and B9 `VBUS`, A5
//! `CC1` and B5 `CC2`, A6 `DP1` and B6 `DP2` (D+), A7 `DN1` and B7 `DN2` (D-), A8 `SBU1` and B8
//! `SBU2`, A12 and B1 `GND`. A signal that two contacts carry is one pin here, since the
//! receptacle joins the two inside (the plug's orientation picks one of them): `.vbus` has four
//! pads, `.gnd` four, `.dp` two (A6, B6) and `.dm` two (A7, B7). The shell is the four plated legs,
//! all numbered `S1` (the drawing gives them no number and the board's footprint calls them S1),
//! one pin. The board's `.shell` is its ground. `.vbus` is the rail of the VBUS and GND contacts: the
//! contacts are the rail's `pos` and `neg`, so a board can state the supply's voltage and the
//! DC analysis can start from it (the host is the receptacle's source).
//!
//! It is a provider of the standard generic `UsbCSinkReceptacle` (ADR 0068), so the board uses the
//! standard `UsbCSink` module and takes this receptacle for it by stating the package `"SMD"` and
//! the number: the standard receptacle has no pin table for that package.

import std::parts::connector::{Connector, UsbCSinkReceptacle}

/// A USB Type-C receptacle with 16 contacts for USB 2.0 and a shell, the Shouhan one that
/// `UsbCSink` takes for the package `"SMD"`. The generic gives it `.vbus` (a rail: `.vbus.pos`
/// and `.vbus.neg`, taken by the DC analysis as a source over the range the design states for
/// `.voltage`), `.package` and `.mpn`; the pins are `.cc1`, `.cc2`, `.dp`, `.dm`, `.sbu1`, `.sbu2`
/// and the shell, whose row is `.shield` (the maker's name) and which the generic calls `.shell`.
part ShouhanTypeC16Pin provides UsbCSinkReceptacle, Connector {
    pins "SMD" {
        //  pin          kind           name       pads
        .vbus.pos power         "VBUS"     "A4" "A9" "B4" "B9"
        .vbus.neg power         "GND"      "A1" "A12" "B1" "B12"
        .cc1    passive       "CC1"      "A5"
        .cc2    passive       "CC2"      "B5"
        .dp     bidirectional "D+"       "A6" "B6"
        .dm     bidirectional "D-"       "A7" "B7"
        .sbu1   passive       "SBU1"     "A8"
        .sbu2   passive       "SBU2"     "B8"
        .shield passive       "SHIELD"   "S1"
    }
    .shell ~ .shield

    catalog shouhan_type_c_16pin by .mpn { .mpn, .package }
}
